First, determine Sophia’s fuel efficiency (miles per gallon).

\[
\text{Miles per gallon} = \frac{\text{Miles traveled}}{\text{Gallons used}}
= \frac{100\text{ miles}}{4\text{ gallons}}
= 25\text{ mpg}
\]

Next, find how many miles she can drive on a full 12‑gallon tank.

\[
\text{Miles per tank} = \text{Miles per gallon} \times \text{Tank capacity}
= 25\text{ mpg} \times 12\text{ gallons}
= 300\text{ miles}
\]

Answer: 300
